# Disclosure matrix collusion check.
# The join over the filled disclosure matrix, mechanised rather than argued in
# prose. Reproduce: python3 scripts/collusion-check.py
#
# Controls. A check whose mitigations can be switched off without changing the
# output is not checking them. Three toggles, three differentials:
#   --no-inv24  3 -> 4 derived leaks   deanonymisation appears, held by {iss} alone
#   --no-rule1  3 -> 4 derived leaks   pre-trade order intent appears, held by {nodes}
#   --no-pool   R17 moves {relay}exact -> {pub}exact

the disclosure matrix COLLUSION CHECK
==========================================================================
rows: 18   parties: 7   subsets checked: 63
Rule 1 (commitments for hidden values): ON
Section 7.5 account pool:               ON

AXIS FINDING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  `relay` (the sponsoring relay) is used by this check and is NOT in
  the observer axis. J4 is a subset containing it
  and the security model's section 6.1 carries it as adversary A5.

PART 1 - PER-ROW JOINS AGAINST CEILING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  subsets containing no party entitled to the row

  R6  Quantity                           {nodes}          exact@pre > bucket
  R12 Counterparty relationship          {pub}            exact@imm > none  <- named unsolved  (public, so every party holds it)
       THE CELL WE DID NOT SOLVE. Settlement runs the stock ATS transfer path (D-05, D-07), which discloses the pair. Should sit at {reg,cp}. Fix is D-08's order-book-only second layer, on the roadmap.
  R15 Activity fingerprint               {nodes}          exact@pre > agg
  R16 Cadence                            {pub}            exact@imm > bucket  (public, so every party holds it)
  R17 Account provenance                 {relay}          exact@imm > bucket

PART 2 - EMERGENT ROW JOINS (strictly more than any member alone)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  none. No row is reconstructed by pooling that a member did not
  already hold. Every row-level leak above is one party's alone,
  which is why part 3 is where the design is actually tested.

PART 3 - DERIVED FACTS (the check a cell-by-cell review cannot do)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Counterparty graph
       held by {iss}   (permitted: {cp u reg u ven})
       inputs: R1>=exact, R12>=exact
       F4-ROW-SCOPE derived fact 1, reconstructed on mainnet.

  Activity fingerprint
       held by {iss}   (permitted: {cp u reg u ven})
       inputs: R1>=exact, R6>=bucket, R16>=exact
       F4-ROW-SCOPE derived fact 2. Identity plus quantity plus time.

  Fund flow per share class
       held by {nodes}   (permitted: {cp u iss u reg u ven})
       inputs: R6>=exact, R7>=exact
       F4-ROW-SCOPE derived fact 3. Scoped to the issuer, not the trader.

==========================================================================
rows checked:                                  18
row-level ceiling violations (minimal):        5
emergent row joins:                            0
derived facts outside their permitted set:     3
rows at ceiling `none` and violated:           R12

Read this as the design intends: the failures below are the ones the
documents already name and price. A check that finds nothing has not
been run against a real design.

=================== CONTROL: --no-inv24 ===================
PART 3 - DERIVED FACTS (the check a cell-by-cell review cannot do)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Deanonymisation: real identity behind a nullifier
       held by {iss}   (permitted: nobody unilaterally)
       inputs: R1>=exact, R11>=exact, R18>=exact
       J4. The issuer holds identity to credential; the registry publishes address to nullifier. The missing edge is cid to n, and INV-24's proof of possession on pk_D = pk_I + pk_V is what keeps it missing.

  Counterparty graph
       held by {iss}   (permitted: {cp u reg u ven})
       inputs: R1>=exact, R12>=exact
       F4-ROW-SCOPE derived fact 1, reconstructed on mainnet.

  Activity fingerprint
       held by {iss}   (permitted: {cp u reg u ven})
       inputs: R1>=exact, R6>=bucket, R16>=exact
       F4-ROW-SCOPE derived fact 2. Identity plus quantity plus time.

  Fund flow per share class
       held by {nodes}   (permitted: {cp u iss u reg u ven})
       inputs: R6>=exact, R7>=exact
       F4-ROW-SCOPE derived fact 3. Scoped to the issuer, not the trader.

